{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>He did not eat bread, etc.</b> It was necessary to specify <b>bread and water</b>, and it would not have sufficed to say 'he did not eat and did not drink,' for if you examine his words carefully, it comes to say that specifically bread and water are what he did not eat and drink, but another kind of eating and another kind of drinking he did eat and drink — as it says (Psalms 40:9): ״וְתוֹרָתְךָ בְּתוֹךְ מֵעָי״, and it is also compared to water (Ta'anit 7a). For had he said 'he did not eat and did not drink,' it would imply every kind of eating and drinking."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:39.362863854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}